# QM5_9165 TradingView Joovier London Session Breakout

## Source
- Source: TradingView Pine script "London Session Breakout - Joovier Gems"
- URL: https://www.tradingview.com/script/JkVblAXK-London-Session-Breakout-Joovier-Gems/
- Author: Joovier Gems (TradingView handle — anon OK under relaxed R1 post-2026-05-15)
- Source landing page: https://www.tradingview.com/scripts/trendanalysis/ (top-trends list, 2026-05-19 snapshot)

## Mechanics

### Entry
- Build a range from the 03:00 ET to 09:00 ET window on the 5-minute chart.
  - `range_high = max(High[t]) for t in [03:00, 09:00] ET`
  - `range_low  = min(Low[t])  for t in [03:00, 09:00] ET`
- Execution window: 09:30 ET to 11:00 ET (London/NY-overlap session).
- **Long**: BUY at market when a 5-minute bar closes with `Close > range_high` inside
  the execution window AND no position is open.
- **Short**: SELL at market when a 5-minute bar closes with `Close < range_low` inside
  the execution window AND no position is open.
- One position per direction per day. First breach wins; no re-entry after stop-out.

### Exit
- Time-stop: flatten at 11:00 ET if neither TP nor SL hit (end of execution window).
- Take-profit: 2R (2 × initial-stop distance) above entry for longs, below for shorts.

### Stop Loss
- Source rule: 5-tick fixed stop. Port to MT5 + DWX: `5 * point` where `point` is the
  symbol's tick size. For EURUSD this is 5 pips (5 × 0.0001 on a 5-digit broker). Codex
  P1 default: `5 * _Point * (_Digits == 5 || _Digits == 3 ? 10 : 1)` so the rule reads
  "5 pips" not "5 ticks of a 0.00001-resolution feed".
- P3 sweep candidate: range-based stop = `0.5 × (range_high - range_low)` as alternative
  when 5-pip is below the typical EURUSD spread+slippage envelope.

### Position Sizing
- V5 standard: `RISK_FIXED = $1,000` for P2 baseline (lots derived from SL distance + tick
  value). `RISK_PERCENT` for live (HR4).

### Additional filters
- Trade only on weekdays (no weekend gaps).
- Skip session if range is < 5 pips (`range_high - range_low < 5 × pip_size`) — flat
  range = no signal.
- Standard V5: QM_KillSwitch, news filter, MAX_DD trip, Friday-close flatten.
- Broker-time conversion: DXZ NY-Close = UTC+2 (UTC+3 during US DST). 03:00-09:00 ET =
  09:00-15:00 broker outside DST, 08:00-14:00 broker during DST. Codex P1 must compute
  this from `TimeGMT()` + DST tables, NOT hard-code the broker offset.

